# Nougat extraction placeholder — arXiv:2107.02789

*Digitized-counterdiabatic quantum approximate optimization algorithm*
P. Chandarana, N. N. Hegade, K. Paul, F. Albarrán-Arriagada, E. Solano, A. del Campo, X. Chen.
arXiv:2107.02789v3 (2022); Phys. Rev. Research 4, 013141 (2022).

This file is a placeholder for a future full-paper Nougat OCR pass (nougat is the transformer-based scientific-document OCR that produces MMD / MathML-annotated markdown). The replication used direct PDF read (`work/paper.pdf`) plus a plain-text dump (`work/paper.txt`) for the sections needed to extract the QAOA + DC-QAOA ansatz specification (§II) and the MaxCut CD pool (§III / Eq. 9).

## Sections consumed during replication (from work/paper.txt)
- §I  — Introduction (motivation: shortcut-to-adiabaticity applied to QAOA)
- §II — DC-QAOA algorithm: standard QAOA layer + counterdiabatic unitary
- §III — Applications: Ising, MaxCut, SK, p-spin; CD operator pools per problem
- Fig. 2 — LFIM 12-qubit R vs p (claim C1, not tested here)
- Fig. 3a — Small-MaxCut R at fixed p (claim C2, tested and REPLICATED on K₄)
- Fig. 3b — MaxCut R vs p depth scaling (claim C3, tested and REPLICATED on n=6, n=8)
- Eq. 9 — CD operator pool {Z⊗Y, Y⊗Z} for MaxCut (claim C4, implemented as specified)

## To upgrade this stub to a full Nougat extraction
```
# small-batch uicgpu A100 route (per TOOLS.md OCR rule)
nougat work/paper.pdf -o extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base --recompute --markdown
mv extraction/paper.mmd extraction/nougat.mmd
```
Expected size ~40–60 KB of MMD-formatted markdown with embedded equations.
This was not run for QC-100 replication because the manual text extraction from `work/paper.txt` was sufficient to identify the ansatz and CD pool; nougat MMD is only needed if a downstream task requires structured equation parsing.
